<section class="card" id="p3">
  <h2>Page 3</h2>
  <div class="en">What Is a Lipid?

Core definition:
Lipids are a heterogeneous group of naturally occurring organic compounds classified together mainly because of their common solubility properties.
Or simply:
Lipids are organic compounds formed mainly from alcohol and fatty acids combined by ester linkage.

Solubility profile:
- Insoluble in water
- Soluble in organic solvents

Common solvents:
- Diethyl ether
- Chloroform
- Acetone

KEY POINT: Many lipid properties begin with one idea: water avoidance.</div>
  <div class="ar">إيه هو الـ Lipid؟ تعريف أساسي: الدهون مجموعة غير متجانسة heterogeneous من مركبات عضوية طبيعية، بتتصنف مع بعض بشكل رئيسي بسبب خواص الذوبان solubility المشتركة. أو ببساطة: مركبات عضوية تتكون أساسًا من كحول alcohol وأحماض دهنية fatty acids متصلة برابطة إستر ester linkage. الذوبان: لا تذوب في الماء insoluble in water، وتذوب في المذيبات العضوية organic solvents. أمثلة مذيبات: diethyl ether و chloroform و acetone. النقطة المهمة: كثير من خواص الدهون تبدأ من فكرة واحدة: تجنب الماء water avoidance.</div>
  <div class="ex">💡 الدهون زي الزيت: لو حطيت زيت في ماء، مش هيختلط بيه ويفضل فوق. عشان كده بنقول إنها بتتجنب الماء water avoidance وبتدور على مذيب عضوي زي الإيثر أو الكلوروفورم.</div>
  <h3>🧠 5 أسئلة على الصفحة</h3>
  <div class="q"><b>1) Why are lipids classified together?</b><div class="opt">A. Common solubility properties</div><div class="opt">B. Same molecular weight</div><div class="opt">C. Same number of carbons</div><div class="opt">D. Identical functions</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: Common solubility properties</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>2) Lipids are generally:</b><div class="opt">A. Insoluble in water and soluble in organic solvents</div><div class="opt">B. Soluble in water and insoluble in organic solvents</div><div class="opt">C. Soluble in both water and organic solvents</div><div class="opt">D. Insoluble in both water and organic solvents</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: Insoluble in water and soluble in organic solvents</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>3) Which of the following is listed as a common lipid solvent?</b><div class="opt">A. Diethyl ether</div><div class="opt">B. Water</div><div class="opt">C. Ethanol only</div><div class="opt">D. Sodium chloride solution</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: Diethyl ether</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>4) In the simple definition, lipids are formed mainly from:</b><div class="opt">A. Alcohol and fatty acids combined by ester linkage</div><div class="opt">B. Sugar and phosphate combined by glycosidic linkage</div><div class="opt">C. Amino acids combined by peptide bonds</div><div class="opt">D. Nucleotides combined by phosphodiester bonds</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: Alcohol and fatty acids combined by ester linkage</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>5) The KEY POINT states that many lipid properties begin with:</b><div class="opt">A. Water avoidance</div><div class="opt">B. Protein folding</div><div class="opt">C. DNA replication</div><div class="opt">D. Enzyme inhibition</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: Water avoidance</div></details></div></div>
</section>
<section class="card" id="p4">
  <h2>Page 4</h2>
  <div class="en">The Four Major Lipid Categories

1. Simple lipids: Alcohol + fatty acids
2. Compound lipids: Lipid + additional group
3. Substances associated with lipids: Vitamins, steroids, carotenes
4. Derived lipids: Hydrolysis products

KEY POINT: Classification depends on what is attached to the lipid framework.</div>
  <div class="ar">التصنيفات الأربعة الرئيسية للدهون:
1. Simple lipids: كحول + أحماض دهنية.
2. Compound lipids: دهن + مجموعة إضافية additional group.
3. Substances associated with lipids: فيتامينات vitamins، ستيرويدات steroids، كاروتينات carotenes.
4. Derived lipids: نواتج التحلل المائي hydrolysis products.
النقطة المهمة: التصنيف بيعتمد على إيه اللي متصل بالهيكل الدهني lipid framework.</div>
  <div class="ex">💡 تخيل الدهن زي شاسيه عربية: لو عليه بس عجل وموتور يبقى simple، لو زودت عليه صندوق إضافي يبقى compound، ولو بتتكلم عن قطع غيار نتجت من فك العربية يبقى derived.</div>
  <h3>🧠 5 أسئلة على الصفحة</h3>
  <div class="q"><b>1) Simple lipids are composed of:</b><div class="opt">A. Alcohol + fatty acids</div><div class="opt">B. Lipid + phosphate group</div><div class="opt">C. Vitamins + steroids</div><div class="opt">D. Proteins + carbohydrates</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: Alcohol + fatty acids</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>2) Compound lipids are described as:</b><div class="opt">A. Lipid + additional group</div><div class="opt">B. Alcohol + fatty acids only</div><div class="opt">C. Hydrolysis products only</div><div class="opt">D. Vitamins and carotenes only</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: Lipid + additional group</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>3) Which of the following are listed as substances associated with lipids?</b><div class="opt">A. Vitamins, steroids, carotenes</div><div class="opt">B. Phospholipids, glycolipids, sulfolipids</div><div class="opt">C. Fatty acids, alcohols, hydrocarbons</div><div class="opt">D. Glycerol, triglycerides, waxes</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: Vitamins, steroids, carotenes</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>4) Derived lipids are best described as:</b><div class="opt">A. Hydrolysis products</div><div class="opt">B. Transport proteins</div><div class="opt">C. Simple esters of glycerol</div><div class="opt">D. Storage polysaccharides</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: Hydrolysis products</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>5) According to the KEY POINT, lipid classification depends on:</b><div class="opt">A. What is attached to the lipid framework</div><div class="opt">B. The color of the lipid</div><div class="opt">C. The temperature of the body</div><div class="opt">D. The presence of water</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: What is attached to the lipid framework</div></details></div></div>
</section>
<section class="card" id="p5">
  <h2>Page 5</h2>
  <div class="en">I. Simple Lipids: The Basic Framework

Simple = only two building blocks:
Alcohol + Fatty acids

Main types are determined by the alcohol component.

Neutral fats:
- Alcohol = glycerol
- Fats are solid; oils are liquid

Waxes:
- Alcohol = higher alcohol, not glycerol

KEY POINT: Simple lipids contain no extra phosphate, carbohydrate or protein group.</div>
  <div class="ar">الدهون البسيطة simple lipids: تتكون من مكونين أساسيين فقط: كحول alcohol + أحماض دهنية fatty acids. الأنواع الرئيسية بتتحدد حسب نوع الكحول. Neutral fats: الكحول هو glycerol، والدهون fats بتكون صلبة solid بينما الزيوت oils سائلة liquid. Waxes: الكحول كحول أعلى higher alcohol وليس glycerol. النقطة المهمة: الدهون البسيطة لا تحتوي على فوسفات phosphate أو كربوهيدرات carbohydrate أو بروتين protein إضافي.</div>
  <div class="ex">💡 زي ساندويتش فيه عيش وحشوة بس: الكحول هو العيش، والأحماض الدهنية هي الحشوة. لو زودت جبنة أو فوسفات، يبقى مش simple.</div>
  <h3>🧠 5 أسئلة على الصفحة</h3>
  <div class="q"><b>1) Simple lipids are made of how many main building blocks?</b><div class="opt">A. Two: alcohol and fatty acids</div><div class="opt">B. Three: glycerol, phosphate and choline</div><div class="opt">C. Four: sugar, phosphate, alcohol and fatty acid</div><div class="opt">D. One: fatty acid only</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: Two: alcohol and fatty acids</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>2) In simple lipids, the main type is determined by:</b><div class="opt">A. The alcohol component</div><div class="opt">B. The phosphate group</div><div class="opt">C. The protein content</div><div class="opt">D. The number of double bonds only</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: The alcohol component</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>3) Neutral fats contain which alcohol?</b><div class="opt">A. Glycerol</div><div class="opt">B. Higher alcohol</div><div class="opt">C. Sphingosine</div><div class="opt">D. Cholesterol</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: Glycerol</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>4) Waxes contain:</b><div class="opt">A. Higher alcohol, not glycerol</div><div class="opt">B. Glycerol only</div><div class="opt">C. Phosphate and glycerol</div><div class="opt">D. Carbohydrate and protein</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: Higher alcohol, not glycerol</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>5) Simple lipids contain no extra:</b><div class="opt">A. Phosphate, carbohydrate or protein group</div><div class="opt">B. Carbon or hydrogen</div><div class="opt">C. Oxygen or nitrogen</div><div class="opt">D. Fatty acid or alcohol</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: Phosphate, carbohydrate or protein group</div></details></div></div>
</section>
<section class="card" id="p6">
  <h2>Page 6</h2>
  <div class="en">II. Compound Lipids

- Phospholipids: Phosphate group
- Glycolipids: Carbohydrate residue
- Sulfolipids: Sulfur-containing group
- Aminolipids: Amino group
- Lipoproteins: Combined with proteins; transport in blood

KEY POINT: Compound lipids gain new properties from the additional chemical group.</div>
  <div class="ar">الدهون المركبة compound lipids:
- Phospholipids: فيها مجموعة فوسفات phosphate.
- Glycolipids: فيها بقايا كربوهيدرات carbohydrate residue.
- Sulfolipids: فيها مجموعة تحتوي على كبريت sulfur-containing group.
- Aminolipids: فيها مجموعة أمينو amino group.
- Lipoproteins: متحدة مع بروتينات proteins، ووظيفتها النقل في الدم transport in blood.
النقطة المهمة: الدهون المركبة بتكتسب خواص جديدة من المجموعة الكيميائية الإضافية additional chemical group.</div>
  <div class="ex">💡 تخيل الدهن زي موبايل: لو ضفت كاميرا، بقى له خاصية تصوير. كل مجموعة إضافية في compound lipids بتدي خاصية جديدة.</div>
  <h3>🧠 5 أسئلة على الصفحة</h3>
  <div class="q"><b>1) Phospholipids contain:</b><div class="opt">A. A phosphate group</div><div class="opt">B. Only a carbohydrate residue</div><div class="opt">C. A sulfur-containing group</div><div class="opt">D. Only an amino group</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: A phosphate group</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>2) Glycolipids are characterized by:</b><div class="opt">A. A carbohydrate residue</div><div class="opt">B. A phosphate group</div><div class="opt">C. An amino group</div><div class="opt">D. A protein only</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: A carbohydrate residue</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>3) Sulfolipids contain:</b><div class="opt">A. A sulfur-containing group</div><div class="opt">B. A phosphate group</div><div class="opt">C. A carbohydrate residue</div><div class="opt">D. Glycerol only</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: A sulfur-containing group</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>4) Lipoproteins are combined with proteins and function in:</b><div class="opt">A. Transport in blood</div><div class="opt">B. Storing fat in adipose tissue</div><div class="opt">C. Digesting proteins</div><div class="opt">D. Synthesizing DNA</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: Transport in blood</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>5) According to the KEY POINT, compound lipids gain new properties from:</b><div class="opt">A. The additional chemical group</div><div class="opt">B. The absence of fatty acids</div><div class="opt">C. The presence of only glycerol</div><div class="opt">D. The absence of alcohol</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: The additional chemical group</div></details></div></div>
</section>
<section class="card" id="p7">
  <h2>Page 7</h2>
  <div class="en">III. Derived Lipids: Products of Hydrolysis

Hydrolysis of simple or compound lipids yields smaller lipid-derived components.

- Fatty acids: Saturated or unsaturated
- Alcohols: Glycerol or higher alcohols
- Hydrocarbons: Hydrocarbon products

KEY POINT: Hydrolysis breaks lipid molecules into fatty acids, alcohols and hydrocarbons.</div>
  <div class="ar">الدهون المشتقة derived lipids: هي نواتج التحلل المائي hydrolysis products. التحلل المائي للدهون البسيطة أو المركبة ينتج مكونات أصغر مشتقة من الدهون. تشمل:
- Fatty acids: مشبعة saturated أو غير مشبعة unsaturated.
- Alcohols: glycerol أو كحولات أعلى higher alcohols.
- Hydrocarbons: نواتج هيدروكربونية hydrocarbon products.
النقطة المهمة: التحلل المائي يكسر جزيئات الدهون إلى أحماض دهنية fatty acids وكحولات alcohols وهيدروكربونات hydrocarbons.</div>
  <div class="ex">💡 زي ما تفكك لعبة تركيب: لو فككت الدهن hydrolysis، هتطلع قطع صغيرة: أحماض دهنية، كحولات، وهيدروكربونات. دي بنسميها derived lipids.</div>
  <h3>🧠 5 أسئلة على الصفحة</h3>
  <div class="q"><b>1) Derived lipids are products of:</b><div class="opt">A. Hydrolysis</div><div class="opt">B. Oxidation only</div><div class="opt">C. Photosynthesis</div><div class="opt">D. Protein synthesis</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: Hydrolysis</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>2) Hydrolysis of simple or compound lipids yields:</b><div class="opt">A. Smaller lipid-derived components</div><div class="opt">B. Larger proteins</div><div class="opt">C. Nucleic acids</div><div class="opt">D. Only vitamins</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: Smaller lipid-derived components</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>3) Fatty acids derived from lipids may be:</b><div class="opt">A. Saturated or unsaturated</div><div class="opt">B. Only saturated</div><div class="opt">C. Only unsaturated</div><div class="opt">D. Always hydrocarbons</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: Saturated or unsaturated</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>4) Alcohols produced by hydrolysis may include:</b><div class="opt">A. Glycerol or higher alcohols</div><div class="opt">B. Only cholesterol</div><div class="opt">C. Only ethanol</div><div class="opt">D. Only methanol</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: Glycerol or higher alcohols</div></details></div></div><div class="q"><b>5) The KEY POINT says hydrolysis breaks lipids into:</b><div class="opt">A. Fatty acids, alcohols and hydrocarbons</div><div class="opt">B. Proteins, sugars and salts</div><div class="opt">C. Nucleotides and amino acids</div><div class="opt">D. Vitamins and minerals</div><div class="det"><details><summary>Show Answer</summary><div class="ok">✅ Correct: Fatty acids, alcohols and hydrocarbons</div></details></div></div>
</section>
<section class="card" id="p8">
  <h2>Page 8</h2>
  <div class="en">IV. Substances Associated with Lipids

Fat-soluble vitamins: A, D, E, K
Steroids: Cholesterol, bile acids, adrenal and sex hormones
Carotenes: Pigment-related lipid-associated compounds

KEY POINT: These substances are lipid-related because of their chemistry or biological association.</div>
  <div class="ar">المواد المرتبطة بالدهون (Substances Associated with Lipids): فيه مجموعات مهمة زي الفيتامينات الذائبة في الدهون (fat-soluble vitamins) وهي A•D•E•K، والستيرويدات (Steroids) زي الكوليسترول (Cholesterol) وأحماض الصفراء (bile acids) وهرمونات الغدة الكظرية والهرمونات الجنسية (adrenal and sex hormones)، والكاروتينات (Carotenes) وهي مركبات مرتبطة بالدهون ومرتبطة بالصبغات. النقطة المهمة: المواد دي تعتبر مرتبطة بالدهون بسبب كيمياءها أو ارتباطها البيولوجي.</div>
  <div class="ex">💡 تخيل الدهون كأنها عصابة ليها أعضاء قريبين منها: فيتامينات A D E K بتدوب فيها، والستيرويدات والكاروتينات بتمشي معاها في نفس الشغل الحيوي.</div>
